+++ b/docs/adr/0002-tags-on-posts.md
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+---
+type: adr
+status: draft
+entities: [Post, Tag, PostTag]
+related:
+  - app/Http/Controllers/PostController.ts
+  - app/Http/Resources/PostResource.ts
+  - app/Http/Validators/PostValidator.ts
+  - db/schema.ts
+generated: { by: "claude-code/claude-fable-5-1", at: 2026-09-29T19:08:31.982Z }
+---
+
+# Tags on posts
+
+## Context
+
+The posts list is one long feed, so readers cannot find posts on a topic.
+Authors tag their posts, tags are shown wherever a post appears, and
+`/posts?tag=<name>` lists the posts carrying one. Topic pages and a tag cloud
+will read the same data, so the names below are a contract.
+
+## Decision
+
+- **Storage.** `tags` (`id`, unique `name`) and `post_tags` (`post_id`,
+  `tag_id`, one row per tag attached to a post; the pair is the primary key).
+  Names are case-sensitive. A tag no post carries stays in `tags`.
+- **The form field stays a string.** `tags` travels as the comma-separated
+  text the author typed. `PostPayloadSchema` checks it without transforming
+  it, and the controller reads the names with `parseTagNames()`: codegen
+  cannot see through a zod transform, so a transforming schema would type the
+  body the controller receives as a string while handing it an array.
+- **Rules.** Names are trimmed, blanks dropped, repeats counted once; after
+  that at most 5 names of 1–30 characters each. A broken rule is a validation
+  failure on `tags`, raised by the route's body schema before the controller
+  runs, so nothing is written.
+- **Writes are one transaction.** `Post.syncTags()` runs in the transaction
+  that creates or updates the post. Deleting a post deletes its `post_tags`
+  rows by hand first: the SQLite connection runs with foreign keys off, so the
+  `ON DELETE CASCADE` on the table cannot be relied on.
+- **Serialization.** Every post `PostResource` serializes carries
+  `tags: string[]`, sorted in code-unit order, `[]` without tags. Every query
+  feeding the resource loads the `tags` relation.
+- **Filtering pages the pivot.** The filtered list paginates the tag's
+  `post_tags` rows by `postId desc` and then loads those posts. Post ids grow
+  with time, so this is the newest-first order of the unfiltered list, and no
+  query holds an IN list of every post carrying the tag. The filter name is
+  not validated against the form rules: an unknown name lists nothing.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Topic pages and the tag cloud can read `tags` and `post_tags` directly.
+- Unused tags accumulate; pruning them is a separate decision.
+- If posts ever stop being listed by id, the filtered list needs a join on the
+  new sort column instead of paging the pivot.
